pt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/staggered/help/figures/README-unnamed-chunk-7-1.png\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'R --vanilla --slave' in /Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/advisor-v2/extreme-stagdid-codex\n exited 2 in 0ms:\n\u001b[1mFatal error: cannot create 'R_TempDir'\r\n\u001b[0m\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/staggered/html/00Index.html && sed -n '1,240p' /opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/staggered/INDEX && sed -n '1,220p' /opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/staggered/DESCRIPTION\" in /Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/advisor-v2/extreme-stagdid-codex\n succeeded in 0ms:\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><title>R: Efficient Estimation Under Staggered Treatment Timing</title>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=yes\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"R.css\" />\n</head><body><div class=\"container\">\n<h1> Efficient Estimation Under Staggered Treatment Timing\n<img class=\"toplogo\" src=\"../../../doc/html/Rlogo.svg\" alt=\"[R logo]\" />\n</h1>\n<hr/>\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<a href=\"../../../doc/html/packages.html\"><img class=\"arrow\" src=\"../../../doc/html/left.jpg\" alt=\"[Up]\" /></a>\n<a href=\"../../../doc/html/index.html\"><img class=\"arrow\" src=\"../../../doc/html/up.jpg\" alt=\"[Top]\" /></a>\n</div><h2>Documentation for package &lsquo;staggered&rsquo; version 1.2.2</h2>\n\n<ul><li><a href=\"../DESCRIPTION\" type=\"text/plain; charset=utf-8\">DESCRIPTION file</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Help Pages</h2>\n\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"balance_checks.html\">balance_checks</a></td>\n<td>Calculate balance checks in staggered rollout designs</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"compute_balance_test.html\">compute_balance_test</a></td>\n<td>Wald-test if Xhat is statistically different from zero</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"compute_Betastar.html\">compute_Betastar</a></td>\n<td>Plug-in efficient Beta hat</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"compute_g_level_summaries.html\">compute_g_level_summaries</a></td>\n<td>Calculate group level summary statistics</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"compute_Xhat.html\">compute_Xhat</a></td>\n<td>Compute Xhat of pre-treatment differences</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"create_A0_list.html\">create_A0_list</a></td>\n<td>create_A0_list</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"pj_officer_level_balanced.html\">pj_officer_level_balanced</a></td>\n<td>Procedural Justice Training Program in the Chicago Police Department</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"staggered.html\">staggered</a></td>\n<td>Calculate the efficient adjusted estimator in staggered rollout designs</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"staggered_cs.html\">staggered_cs</a></td>\n<td>Calculate the Callaway &amp; Sant'Anna (2021) estimator for staggered rollouts</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"staggered_sa.html\">staggered_sa</a></td>\n<td>Calculate the Sun &amp; Abraham (2020) estimator for staggered rollouts</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div></body></html>\nbalance_checks          Calculate balance checks in staggered rollout\n                        designs\ncompute_Betastar        Plug-in efficient Beta hat\ncompute_Xhat            Compute Xhat of pre-treatment differences\ncompute_balance_test    Wald-test if Xhat is statistically different\n                        from zero\ncompute_g_level_summaries\n                        Calculate group level summary statistics\ncreate_A0_list          create_A0_list\npj_officer_level_balanced\n                        Procedural Justice Training Program in the\n                        Chicago Police Department\nstaggered               Calculate the efficient adjusted estimator in\n                        staggered rollout designs\nstaggered_cs            Calculate the Callaway & Sant'Anna (2021)\n                        estimator for staggered rollouts\nstaggered_sa            Calculate the Sun & Abraham (2020) estimator\n                        for staggered rollouts\nPackage: staggered\nTitle: Efficient Estimation Under Staggered Treatment Timing\nVersion: 1.2.2\nAuthors@R: \n    c(person(\"Jonathan\", \"Roth\", email = \"jonathan_roth@brown.edu\", role = c(\"aut\")),\n    person(\"Pedro H.C.\", \"Sant'Anna\", email = \"pedrohcgs@gmail.com\", role = c(\"aut\",\"cre\")))\nDescription: Efficiently estimates treatment effects in settings with randomized staggered rollouts, using tools \n    proposed by Roth and Sant'Anna (2023) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2102.01291>.\nLicense: GPL-2\nEncoding: UTF-8\nLazyData: true\nRoxygenNote: 7.3.2\nImports: data.table, purrr, Rcpp, RcppEigen, magrittr, MASS, stats\nLinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen\nDepends: R (>= 3.5.0)\nNeedsCompilation: yes\nPackaged: 2025-01-09 18:38:57 UTC; pedrosantanna\nAuthor: Jonathan Roth [aut],\n  Pedro H.C. Sant'Anna [aut, cre]\nMaintainer: Pedro H.C. Sant'Anna <pedrohcgs@gmail.com>\nRepository: CRAN\nDate/Publication: 2025-01-09 19:00:02 UTC\nBuilt: R 4.5.1; aarch64-apple-darwin24.4.0; 2026-07-17 12:17:36 UTC; unix\n\ncodex\nThe core conclusion is sound, but I would make three changes.\n\n1. Replace the Roth–Sant’Anna `staggered()` estimate with Sun–Abraham. `staggered()` is designed for randomized staggered rollouts, whereas minimum-wage adoption is observational. Treating it as an ordinary parallel-trends robustness estimator is the submission’s main methodological weakness. Use a county-clustered `fixest::sunab` specification and report its aggregated ATT with never-treated counties as the reference group. If retaining Roth–Sant’Anna, explicitly state its stronger assignment assumption and do not use it to validate the causal conclusion.\n\n2. Qualify the cross-estimator comparison. TWFE, C&S simple aggregation, and Sun–Abraham do not generally apply identical weights to cohort-time effects. Their similarity supports robustness of the sign and approximate magnitude; it does not show that TWFE’s negative-weight bias is exactly the difference between −0.0365 and −0.0398.\n\n3. Align the pretrend evidence. The reported `cs_notyet$Wpval` tests all available group-time pre-treatment restrictions, while the graph is truncated at event time −3. Either plot the available −4 lead or state explicitly that the joint test includes pre-treatment cells not displayed. I would also describe the result as “no statistically detectable pretrend” rather than positive support for parallel trends, given limited power and changing cohort support across event times.\n\nKeep the Bacon interpretation, including the important clarification that 5.39% is exposure to the problematic comparison type—not a literal negative-weight share. Keep C&S with not-yet-treated controls as the preferred estimate, but report the transformed magnitude precisely as `exp(−0.0398) − 1 ≈ −3.9%`.\n\nA final useful caveat: minimum-wage treatment is assigned at the state level. County clustering follows the brief, but it may understate uncertainty from within-state dependence; acknowledge that limitation even if the required table retains county-level inference.\ntokens used\n49,030\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
